---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const post = {
 title: "New Hire Workwear Checklist for Las Vegas Contractors: What to Order Before Day One",
 description:
 "A practical planning checklist for new construction hires in Las Vegas, with example product categories, sizing questions, and employer safety approvals to gather before ordering.",
 category: 'Operations',
 readTime: '10 min read',
 date: 'Apr 28, 2026',
 isoDate: '2026-04-28',
 image: '/images/generated/kit-gc.jpg',
 imageAlt: 'New hire construction crew kit with embroidered shirts hi-vis vest and Carhartt pants',
 slug: 'new-hire-workwear-checklist-las-vegas-contractors',
}

const schema = {
 '@context': 'https://schema.org',
 '@graph': [
 {
 '@type': 'Article',
 headline: post.title,
 description: post.description,
 image: `https://bighornthreads.com${post.image}`,
 datePublished: post.isoDate,
 dateModified: '2026-08-21',
 author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/about/' },
 publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bighorn Threads', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://bighornthreads.com/images/logos/bighorn-logo-color.png' } },
 mainEntityOfPage: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`,
 },
 {
 '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
 itemListElement: [
 { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/' },
 { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://bighornthreads.com/blog/' },
 { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: post.title, item: `https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/` },
 ],
 },
 ],
}
---

<BaseLayout title={post.title} description={post.description} canonical={`https://bighornthreads.com/blog/${post.slug}/`} ogImage={post.image} type="article" publishedDate={post.isoDate}>
 <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

 <article class="bg-concrete">
 <header class="border-b border-hairline bg-paper">
 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-16 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20 lg:px-8">
 <nav class="mb-6 font-mono text-xs text-ash" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
 <a href="/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Home</a><span class="px-2">/</span><a href="/blog/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Blog</a>
 </nav>
 <span class="kicker mb-3">{post.category}</span>
 <h1 class="mb-6 font-heading text-3xl font-extrabold uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight text-charcoal sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{post.title}</h1>
 <p class="mb-8 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ash">
 A planning checklist for a new hire's apparel. Confirm each product, size, decoration, safety requirement, price, and delivery estimate before ordering.
 </p>
 <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 border-t border-hairline pt-6 font-mono text-sm text-ash">
 <span class="text-gold-600">Bighorn Threads Team</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span>{post.readTime}</span><span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><time datetime={post.isoDate}>{post.date}</time>
 </div>
 </div>
 </header>

 <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <img src={post.image} alt={post.imageAlt} width="1200" height="675" loading="eager" class="w-full border border-hairline object-cover" />
 </div>

 <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 New hires show up Monday. The job started Friday. Your operations manager forwards you their size, hopes for the best, and the new hire spends week one looking like the odd one out — the only person on the crew without branded apparel, while everyone else looks like a unified professional team. That's the gap this checklist exists to close.
 </p>

 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Bighorn Threads can scope a proposed <a href="/company-stores/" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">company-store program</a>. No platform has been selected or launched. Product presentation, size submission, implementation, decoration, delivery, and timing capabilities require separate written approval.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal"><a href="/industries/general-contractors-las-vegas/" class="hover:text-gold-600">General Contractor Field Crew</a></h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 For framers, concrete crews, finish carpenters, and general field labor, the day-one kit is straightforward but should be complete enough that the new hire isn't borrowing or buying their own gear in week one.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>5× Carhartt K87 heavyweight cotton tees, embroidered or screen-printed left chest, in your company colorway</li>
 <li>2× Carhartt B11 work pants or B324 carpenter pants (hemmed if specified)</li>
 <li>1× Carhartt K121 pullover hoodie (for fall/winter starts)</li>
 <li>1× Carhartt 100286 FastDry Logo Cap or Richardson 112 trucker hat with embroidered logo</li>
 <li>Hard-hat decal only after employer and helmet-manufacturer approval</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Ask Bighorn to quote the employer-approved kit. Product availability, pricing, decoration, and lead time require written confirmation.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal"><a href="/industries/electrical-contractors-las-vegas/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Electrical Contractor (FR-Required)</a></h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 The employer's hazard assessment determines whether a new electrical hire needs arc-rated apparel and which rating applies. Bighorn does not prescribe a PPE category.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>Employer-selected arc-rated shirt options with current product documentation</li>
 <li>Employer-selected protective pants when required by the hazard assessment</li>
 <li>Employer-selected high-visibility outerwear when required for the task and site</li>
 <li>1× embroidered Carhartt cap with company logo</li>
 <li>Manufacturer and production-partner documentation requested for the safety binder</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Talk to us for current kit pricing and lead time. <a href="/blog/nfpa-70e-fr-shirts-vegas-electricians/" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">More on NFPA 70E FR selection here</a>.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal"><a href="/industries/plumbing-hvac-las-vegas/" class="hover:text-gold-600">HVAC, Plumbing, Mechanical Service</a></h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Service-trade hires may need a consistent uniform for customer visits. Industrial work shirts with approved logos and name patches are one option to compare.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>5× Red Kap SP14 industrial work shirts (short sleeve summer / long sleeve winter)</li>
 <li>2× Red Kap PT20 industrial work pants (hemmed)</li>
 <li>1× Red Kap JT22 insulated duck work jacket (for fall/winter hires)</li>
 <li>Embroidered company logo (left chest) + woven name patch (right chest)</li>
 <li>1× Richardson 112 trucker hat with embroidered logo</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Talk to us for current kit pricing and lead time. Laundry tagging and delivery depend on written confirmation from the laundry provider and production partner.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Hi-Vis Road, Utility, Paving Crews</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Road and utility employers select the required visibility class from the hazard assessment, project specification, and current standard. Each proposed decoration method and placement must be approved against manufacturer instructions.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>Employer-selected high-visibility shirts with current product documentation</li>
 <li>Employer-selected work pants or supplemental visibility products when required</li>
 <li>Employer-selected high-visibility outerwear for applicable work conditions</li>
 <li>Company logo only in a manufacturer-approved decoration method and placement</li>
 <li>Current garment and decoration documentation requested for the safety binder</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Talk to us for current kit pricing and lead time. <a href="/blog/ansi-107-class-2-vs-class-3-hi-vis-las-vegas/" class="text-gold-700 underline hover:text-gold-600">More on Class 2 vs Class 3 selection here</a>.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal"><a href="/industries/roofing-solar-las-vegas/" class="hover:text-gold-600">Solar EPC and PV Maintenance</a></h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Solar employers determine FR, visibility, and sun-exposure requirements from the task hazard assessment. Product labels and manufacturer documentation must support the approved selection.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>Employer-selected protective shirts when required by the hazard assessment</li>
 <li>Employer-selected protective work pants when required</li>
 <li>Lightweight long-sleeve options with current manufacturer sun-protection documentation</li>
 <li>Employer-selected high-visibility outerwear when required for traffic exposure</li>
 <li>Hard-hat decal only after employer and helmet-manufacturer approval</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Talk to us for current kit pricing and lead time.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Project Manager / Office / Client-Facing</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 PMs, estimators, business development, and ownership may need a different product list. Compare current polo and outerwear options for the role and site.
 </p>
 <ul class="mb-8 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 <li>5× Port Authority K540 Silk Touch Performance polos with embroidered logo + name</li>
 <li>1× Carhartt or Eddie Bauer softshell jacket (for cold-weather walkthroughs)</li>
 <li>1× Carhartt FastDry cap with embroidered logo</li>
 <li>1× embroidered tote bag or backpack for trade-show season</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Talk to us for current kit pricing and lead time.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">Sizing Tips</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 Collect the new hire's measurements and compare them with the current size chart for each exact SKU. Do not assume sizes convert across brands or products. Confirm layering, mobility, and required protective coverage with an approved sample or fit process.
 </p>

 <h2 class="mt-12 mb-4 font-heading text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal">The Company-Store Solution</h2>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-charcoal">
 A company-store workflow may help organize approved products and employee sizes. User access, allowances, HR integration, payment, production, fulfillment, home delivery, timing, reporting, and file retention all depend on the selected configuration and must be confirmed in writing before setup.
 </p>

 <div class="my-12 border border-hairline bg-panel p-8">
 <h3 class="mb-3 font-heading text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-tight text-charcoal">Set up a new-hire kit program</h3>
 <p class="mb-6 text-lg text-ash">
 Workshop call to spec your trade-specific kit. </p>
 <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary text-base">Spec a New Hire Kit</a>
 </div>
 </div>
 </article>
</BaseLayout>
